WEBVTT

00:00:00.676 --> 00:00:02.616
Cross text connections.

00:00:02.616 --> 00:00:04.506
One sentence per author.

00:00:04.506 --> 00:00:05.333
Then compare.

00:00:06.881 --> 00:00:08.761
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:08.761 --> 00:00:11.561
Two short texts on the same topic.

00:00:11.561 --> 00:00:14.651
And a question about how one author would respond to the other.

00:00:15.693 --> 00:00:18.539
It's testing whether you can track two viewpoints at once.

00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:21.117
Here's the method.

00:00:21.117 --> 00:00:23.867
Summarize Text 1 in one sentence.

00:00:23.867 --> 00:00:26.667
Summarize Text 2 in one sentence.

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:31.797
Name the relationship: agree, disagree, or partly agree.

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:34.853
Then answer for the exact point the question asks about.

00:00:35.943 --> 00:00:37.828
Listen for these clues.

00:00:37.828 --> 00:00:42.143
It is true that, followed by but, means partial agreement.

00:00:42.143 --> 00:00:46.383
Whatever they intended concedes one point, and moves to another.

00:00:46.383 --> 00:00:49.238
Text 2 rarely rejects everything.

00:00:49.238 --> 00:00:53.653
Often, the authors agree on the facts, but disagree about the cause.

00:00:54.693 --> 00:00:56.128
Let's try one.

00:00:56.128 --> 00:01:00.728
Text 1 says that learning music improves math, so music is the cause.

00:01:00.728 --> 00:01:07.113
Text 2 agrees that young musicians often excel at math, but says we can't conclude that music is the cause.

00:01:07.113 --> 00:01:10.938
So Text 2 accepts the pattern, but questions the cause.

00:01:10.938 --> 00:01:13.148
Choice A is too extreme.

00:01:13.148 --> 00:01:17.088
Choice C is wrong, because Text 2 accepts the data.

00:01:17.088 --> 00:01:20.458
Choice D agrees with the conclusion of Text 1.

00:01:20.458 --> 00:01:22.714
Choice B matches, so it's the answer.

00:01:23.773 --> 00:01:26.223
Watch out for total disagreement.

00:01:26.223 --> 00:01:30.318
The authors usually clash on one specific point, not on everything.

00:01:31.381 --> 00:01:38.046
Here's the whole lesson on one page: how to spot it, the four steps, the clues, and the trap.

00:01:38.046 --> 00:01:40.879
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
